From 3a4f0c7c3969ec6e25e729ed6b36a0391764a375 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Dmitry V. Levin" <ldv@strace.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strace: handle ESRCH from PTRACE_GETSIGINFO during
 termination

A tracee can become unavailable for ptrace operations after wait4 reports
a signal-delivery-stop, for example when another thread calls exit_group.
PTRACE_GETSIGINFO then fails with ESRCH, which next_event currently treats
as a group-stop.  If the tracee reaches PTRACE_EVENT_EXIT before the
subsequent PTRACE_LISTEN, that request fails with EIO and strace aborts
the trace, killing remaining tracees when kill-on-exit is enabled.

Skip the stale event on ESRCH and let subsequent termination events be
processed normally.  Recognize a group-stop only on EINVAL and diagnose
unexpected errors.  Add synchronized regression tests with and without
seccomp-BPF tracing, forcing the query failure before killing the tracee.

* src/strace.c (next_event): Distinguish EINVAL, ESRCH, and unexpected
PTRACE_GETSIGINFO failures.
* src/disable_ptrace_getsiginfo.c: New helper.
* src/Makefile.am (noinst_PROGRAMS): Add disable_ptrace_getsiginfo.
(disable_ptrace_getsiginfo_LDADD): New variable.
* src/.gitignore: Add /disable_ptrace_getsiginfo.
* tests/getsiginfo-esrch.sh: New common regression test driver.
* tests/Makefile.am (EXTRA_DIST): Add getsiginfo-esrch.sh.
* tests/gen_tests.in (getsiginfo-esrch, getsiginfo-esrch--seccomp-bpf):
New tests.
* NEWS: Mention this fix.

Fixes: v4.7~186 "Add experimental code to use PTRACE_SEIZE, disabled by default"
Resolves: https://github.com/strace/strace/issues/433
Assisted-by: OpenCode:gpt-6.1-sol
